The member-wise copy is already close to optimal, so expect at most a tiny gain. The only change is to skip the `devFields` copy when the source has none, which is the common case for most messages. The result is identical: the vector stays empty, just as copying an empty vector would leave it.

```cpp
Mesg::Mesg(const Mesg &mesg)
    : profile(mesg.profile)
    , localNum(mesg.localNum)
    , fields(mesg.fields)
    , devFields()
{
    if (!mesg.devFields.empty())
        devFields = mesg.devFields;
}
```